# SemText npl-declaration — version/extension banner, all display modes
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house convention). Two example panels in one
# frame, one per display mode the tag provides: the `definition` banner
# (default) and the `extension` banner with its extend-target label. The
# invariant the design must broadcast: the banner is DISPLAY-ONLY chrome —
# a version stamp header above the authored rules — and the rules body
# stays fully readable in every mode (a declaration never occludes its
# body; occlusion belongs to the sem-spoiler / quiz tier).
#
# MODE 1 — definition (default `type`):
#   visible: a full-width banner strip with a 3px violet accent bar on its
#     left edge and a faint violet tint fill; inside it a single mono-font
#     version mark in the accent colour (the `⌜NPL@<version>⌝` stamp —
#     abstract placeholder bars in the mock); below the strip, separated by
#     clear space, the rules body as bright readable prose bars.
#   must never: fill the banner strip opaque; render the mark larger or
#     brighter than the body; run the body into the strip without
#     separation.
# MODE 2 — extension (`type="extension" extend-target="…"`):
#   visible: the identical banner strip; the mark switches to the extend
#     spelling (the mock shows a subtly longer placeholder bar), followed
#     after a small arrow by a trailing small-caps muted label — the
#     extend-target, the vocabulary being extended; same readable rules
#     body below.
#   must never: drop the arrow before the target; render the target as
#     part of the mark or as body prose; restyle the strip differently
#     from mode 1.
#
# Excluded deliberately: the JS-off reading (plain authored prose, no
# banner) — it is the absence of the runtime, not a display mode; the
# schema promises "nothing hidden, nothing generated" for it.
#
# Reference snapshots (snapshot harness ran for this tag):
#   .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-declaration/ — the two harness
#   `-fullpage-` PNGs carry the reference page (attribute table + example
#   viewers); the `render-fixture-*.png` files are component-level renders
#   of both modes (dark 2x, light 2x, mobile 390) against the real
#   vocabulary CSS. Attach before generation.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-declaration
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of two side-by-side reference-page panels
    illustrating one declaration-banner element in its two display modes,
    wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D). Dark
    slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and a
    faint violet radial glow upper-left. Two equal panels sit side by side,
    separated by a thin slate hairline divider, each panel a dark slate
    card (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border, squared corners, deep
    soft shadow; a small dim caption bar sits above each panel.

    Every panel shows the SAME two-part anatomy at its centre. Part one is
    a full-width banner strip: squared 6px corners, a 3px violet (#7C3AED)
    accent bar on its left edge, a hairline slate outline, and a
    barely-there violet tint fill (#7C3AED at 8% opacity over the card).
    Inside the strip, one short line of small monospace-feeling placeholder
    bars in bright violet (#A78BFA) — the version stamp. Part two, below
    the strip with clear separation, is the rules body: two or three
    bright near-white prose bars of differing length — the most prominent,
    fully readable element in the panel. All copy is abstract placeholder
    bars — strictly no letters, digits, or words anywhere.

    Left panel — DEFINITION (default). The banner strip carries only the
    short violet stamp line. Body bars below, untouched.

    Right panel — EXTENSION. The identical strip; the stamp line is one
    bar longer (the extend spelling), and after a small solid violet
    right-pointing arrow it gains a trailing label: one shorter, dimmer
    muted-slate placeholder bar in small-caps scale, clearly separated
    from the stamp. Body bars below, identical to the left panel.

    The two strips must be pixel-comparable: same accent bar, tint,
    outline, and stamp position — the only differences being the longer
    stamp and the arrow + trailing target label on the right. The body
    bars never change between panels.

  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, light mode, white cards, 3D, photorealism,
    faces, avatars, robot mascots, more than two panels, opaque filled
    banner strip, solid color-block hiding the stamp, blurred or dimmed
    body bars, the target label fused with the version stamp, extra chrome
    (badges, counts, buttons, icons)
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, squared corners, hairline
    borders, slate and violet palette, two-panel mode comparison

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-declaration/render-fixture-dark-2x.png
    role: reference
    description: component-level render of both modes, dark theme 2x — banner
      strip anatomy (accent bar, tint, mono stamp, arrow + small-caps target)
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-declaration/render-fixture-light-2x.png
    role: reference
    description: the same two modes in the light theme — token-driven palette
      proof
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-declaration/npl-declaration-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: full reference page — chrome, attribute table, example viewer
      placement

requirements:
  subject: two panels of one declaration banner — left definition (short
    violet stamp in a tinted accent strip), right extension (longer stamp
    plus arrow and trailing small-caps target label); readable rules body
    below the strip in both
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, violet
    accent bar and tint, bright violet mono stamp, near-white body bars,
    muted slate target label
  composition: two equal panels side by side, strips at a consistent
    vertical position, identical body bars across panels
  do:
    - keep the rules body bars the most prominent, most readable element
      in every panel
    - keep the banner strip a faint tint over the card, never opaque
    - differentiate modes only by stamp length and the arrow + target
      label
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, or logos
    - occluding, blurring, or dimming the rules body
    - a target label that reads as part of the version stamp or the body
    - extra chrome (badges, counts, buttons) the tag does not define

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  required_pass:
    - mode_differentiation
    - legibility_invariant
  criteria:
    mode_differentiation:
      weight: 3
      description: Left panel strip carries only the short stamp; right
        strip is one bar longer with arrow + trailing dim small-caps
        label — strips otherwise identical
      fail_signals:
        - arrow or target label present in the left panel
        - target label missing in the right panel
        - strip anatomy (accent bar, tint, corners) differs between panels
    legibility_invariant:
      weight: 3
      description: Body bars are bright, prominent and unoccluded in both
        panels; the strip is tinted, not filled; body clearly separated
        from the strip
      fail_signals:
        - body bars dimmer than the stamp or label
        - opaque or solid strip fill
        - blur, redaction, or occlusion overlays on any body bar
        - body fused into the strip
    theme_fidelity:
      weight: 2
      description: Dark slate + violet, squared hairline panels, flat style
      fail_signals:
        - light theme
        - glossy 3D look
        - rounded card corners
  reject_if:
    - any legible text, letters, digits, watermark, or logo
    - an occluded, blurred, or hidden rules body in either panel
    - more than two panels or a chaotic layout

tags:
  - semtext
  - reference
  - npl-declaration
